A2       CAN ANY OF THESE FIELDS CONTAIN Q(sqrt-3)?  -- the load-bearing half
         TWO INDEPENDENT REASONS, each decisive on its own:
           (i) [Q(sqrt-3):Q] = 2, so a field containing it has EVEN degree over Q.
               A CUBIC field therefore cannot contain it -- 2 does not divide 3.
           (ii) Q(sqrt-3) is imaginary quadratic.  If sigma: K -> R is a REAL embedding
               and Q(sqrt-3) is a subfield of K, then sigma(sqrt-3) is a real number
               whose square is -3.  Impossible.  So a field with ANY real embedding
               cannot contain Q(sqrt-3).
         m003(-3,1)   degree 3 (odd: True), real embeddings: 1 -> CANNOT contain Q(sqrt-3): True
         m004(6,1)    degree 3 (odd: True), real embeddings: 1 -> CANNOT contain Q(sqrt-3): True
         m004(8,1)    degree 3 (odd: True), real embeddings: 1 -> CANNOT contain Q(sqrt-3): True
         m004(5,1)    UNDETERMINED -- no claim made
         m004(7,1)    UNDETERMINED -- no claim made
         SO: for every field this arc DETERMINED, the selecting field is excluded twice
         over.  The relayed conclusion -- 'no closing carries the selecting field' --
         is CONFIRMED where it could be checked, INDEPENDENTLY OF ARITHMETICITY.

A3       B288's LOCK -- DIAGNOSED, AND DELIBERATELY NOT REPAIRED
         tests/test_b288_*.py asserts:
             def test_no_closed_filling_is_arithmetic():
                 assert b288.N_ARITHMETIC == 0   # none imaginary-quadratic; ...
         THE COMMENT CONTAINS THE BUG.  'None imaginary-quadratic' is the criterion for
         a CUSPED group.  A CLOSED filling must be judged by the COCOMPACT criterion
         (Maclachlan-Reid 8.3.2: one complex place, integral traces, the invariant
         quaternion algebra ramified at every real place).  So:
           - the test's NAME asserts something FALSE;
           - what it actually verifies -- no closed filling has an imaginary-quadratic
             invariant trace field -- is TRUE, and is the load-bearing half A2 confirms.
         A test that certifies a falsehood is worse than no test, so this is recorded
         as a live defect.  IT IS NOT REPAIRED HERE: B1376 on the paper lane is that
         seat's active repair, and duplicating it would be exactly the collision this
         record has already been bitten by (the B1267 renumber).  FLAGGED, NOT TAKEN.

